<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Computation and memory analysis of <span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net </span>without re-computation</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present a detailed computation and memory analysis of <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net</span>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Transformer layers with LLaMA architecture</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to make a comparsion with other efficient methods, the computation and memory analysis are based on LLaMA framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> transformer layers. Here, we focus on the forward- and backward-propagation of <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net</span>. It should be reminded that we omit the layer normalization, rotary position embedding, and in-layer residual for simply.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward Propagation. </span>For the input <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times h}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the sequence length and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the hidden dimension. For the first layer, the transformer block’s attention mechanism implements a series of linear transformations through three fundamental computational stages:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{1}^{\text{Q}}=X_{1}W_{1}^{\text{Q}},\quad Y_{1}^{\text{K}}=X_{1}W_{1}^{\text{K}},\quad Y_{1}^{\text{V}}=X_{1}W_{1}^{\text{V}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{1}^{\text{Q}}=X_{1}W_{1}^{\text{Q}},\quad Y_{1}^{\text{K}}=X_{1}W_{1}^{\text{K}},\quad Y_{1}^{\text{V}}=X_{1}W_{1}^{\text{V}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}^{\text{Q}},W_{1}^{\text{K}},W_{1}^{\text{V}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}^{\text{Q}},W_{1}^{\text{K}},W_{1}^{\text{V}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> are full-size weight parameters. For the other layers, the weight matrices of linear transformations are replaced by low-rank weights and the cross-layer residual should also be taken:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{l}^{\text{Q}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{Q}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{Q}}+X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{Q}}B_{l}^{\text{Q}},\quad Y_{l}^{\text{K}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{K}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{K}}+X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{K}}B_{l}^{\text{K}},\quad Y_{l}^{\text{V}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{V}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{V}}+X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{V}}B_{l}^{\text{V}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{l}^{\text{Q}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{Q}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{Q}}+X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{Q}}B_{l}^{\text{Q}},\quad Y_{l}^{\text{K}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{K}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{K}}+X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{K}}B_{l}^{\text{K}},\quad Y_{l}^{\text{V}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{V}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{V}}+X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{V}}B_{l}^{\text{V}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}^{\text{Q}},A_{l}^{\text{K}},A_{l}^{\text{V}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}^{\text{Q}},A_{l}^{\text{K}},A_{l}^{\text{V}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}^{\text{Q}},B_{l}^{\text{K}},B_{l}^{\text{V}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}^{\text{Q}},B_{l}^{\text{K}},B_{l}^{\text{V}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> are low-rank parameter matrices. Then for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,2,\cdots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,2,\cdots,L</annotation></semantics></math>, the immediate activations can be combined as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{l}^{\text{s}}=Y_{l}^{\text{Q}}(Y_{l}^{\text{K}})^{\top},\quad\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}=\text{softmax}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{l}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right),\quad\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}=\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}Y_{l}^{\text{V}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mtext>Att</mtext><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mtext>Att</mtext><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{l}^{\text{s}}=Y_{l}^{\text{Q}}(Y_{l}^{\text{K}})^{\top},\quad\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}=\text{softmax}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{l}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right),\quad\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}=\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}Y_{l}^{\text{V}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Then for the first layer, the attention output can be obtained by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{1}^{\text{O}}=\text{Att}_{1}^{\text{h}}W_{1}^{\text{O}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mn>1</mn><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{1}^{\text{O}}=\text{Att}_{1}^{\text{h}}W_{1}^{\text{O}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}^{\text{O}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}^{\text{O}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the full-size output matrix. For <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=2,3,\cdots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=2,3,\cdots,L</annotation></semantics></math>, the attention output can be obtained by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{l}^{\text{O}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{O}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{O}}+\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}A_{l}^{\text{O}}B_{l}^{\text{O}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{l}^{\text{O}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{O}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{O}}+\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}A_{l}^{\text{O}}B_{l}^{\text{O}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}^{\text{O}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}^{\text{O}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}^{\text{O}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}^{\text{O}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the low-rank parameter matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, the feed-forward network consists of three linear layers. Among them, the gate layer and up-projection layer are computed in layer 1 as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{1}^{\text{gate}}=Y_{1}^{\text{O}}W_{1}^{\text{gate}},\quad Y_{1}^{\text{up}}=Y_{1}^{\text{O}}W_{1}^{\text{up}},\quad X_{1}^{\text{down}}=\text{silu}(Y_{1}^{\text{gate}})\odot Y_{1}^{\text{up}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>silu</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{1}^{\text{gate}}=Y_{1}^{\text{O}}W_{1}^{\text{gate}},\quad Y_{1}^{\text{up}}=Y_{1}^{\text{O}}W_{1}^{\text{up}},\quad X_{1}^{\text{down}}=\text{silu}(Y_{1}^{\text{gate}})\odot Y_{1}^{\text{up}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}^{\text{gate}},W_{1}^{\text{up}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times h_{\text{ff}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}^{\text{gate}},W_{1}^{\text{up}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times h_{\text{ff}}}</annotation></semantics></math> are full-size weight matrices. For the other layer, it can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{l}^{\text{gate}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{gate}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{gate}}+Y_{l}^{\text{O}}A_{l}^{\text{gate}}B_{l}^{\text{gate}},\quad Y_{l}^{\text{up}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{up}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{up}}+Y_{l}^{\text{O}}A_{l}^{\text{up}}B_{l}^{\text{up}},\quad X_{l}^{\text{down}}=\text{silu}(Y_{l}^{\text{gate}})\odot Y_{l}^{\text{up}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>silu</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{l}^{\text{gate}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{gate}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{gate}}+Y_{l}^{\text{O}}A_{l}^{\text{gate}}B_{l}^{\text{gate}},\quad Y_{l}^{\text{up}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{up}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{up}}+Y_{l}^{\text{O}}A_{l}^{\text{up}}B_{l}^{\text{up}},\quad X_{l}^{\text{down}}=\text{silu}(Y_{l}^{\text{gate}})\odot Y_{l}^{\text{up}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}^{\text{gate}},A_{l}^{\text{up}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}^{\text{gate}},A_{l}^{\text{up}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}^{\text{gate}},B_{l}^{\text{up}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h_{\text{ff}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}^{\text{gate}},B_{l}^{\text{up}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h_{\text{ff}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote low-rank parameters and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the element-wise production. Finally, the down-projection in the first layer can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{1}^{\text{down}}=X_{1}^{\text{down}}W_{1}^{\text{down}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{1}^{\text{down}}=X_{1}^{\text{down}}W_{1}^{\text{down}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h_{\text{ff}}\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h_{\text{ff}}\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> are full-size weight matrices. For the other layer, it can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{l}^{\text{down}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{down}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{down}}+X_{l}^{\text{down}}A_{l}^{\text{down}}B_{l}^{\text{down}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{l}^{\text{down}}=\beta_{l}^{\text{down}}Y_{l-1}^{\text{down}}+X_{l}^{\text{down}}A_{l}^{\text{down}}B_{l}^{\text{down}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h_{\text{ff}}\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h_{\text{ff}}\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> denote low-rank parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backward Propagation. </span>
For a matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and the loss function <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we use <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}M:=\frac{\partial\ell}{\partial M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}M:=\frac{\partial\ell}{\partial M}</annotation></semantics></math>. To compute the gradients of all the parameters in layer <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, the back propagation begins with the partial gradient of the loss function <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the input of the next layer, i.e., <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}X_{l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}X_{l+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Then, for the last layer, the gradient of the output holds that <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{down}}=\mathcal{D}X_{L+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{down}}=\mathcal{D}X_{L+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{L+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{L+1}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the input of output layers. However, for the other layer, it holds that:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{down}}=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{down}}\mathcal{D}Y_{l+1}^{\text{down}}+\mathcal{D}X_{L+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{down}}=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{down}}\mathcal{D}Y_{l+1}^{\text{down}}+\mathcal{D}X_{L+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For the first layer, the gradient of inputs and weights for down-projection can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}X_{1}^{\text{down}}=\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{down}}(W_{1}^{\text{down}})^{\top},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{down}}=(X_{1}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{down}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}X_{1}^{\text{down}}=\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{down}}(W_{1}^{\text{down}})^{\top},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{down}}=(X_{1}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{down}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">For the other layers, the gradient of inputs and weights for down-projection can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}X_{l}^{\text{down}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}X_{l}^{\text{down}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{down}}(A_{l}^{\text{down}}B_{l}^{\text{down}})^{\top},\quad\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{down}}=(X_{l}^{\text{down}}A_{l}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{down}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{down}}(A_{l}^{\text{down}}B_{l}^{\text{down}})^{\top},\quad\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{down}}=(X_{l}^{\text{down}}A_{l}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{down}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E22Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{down}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{down}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(X_{l}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{down}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(X_{l}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{down}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For the last layer, as the gradient of activations do not rely on the former layers. Thus the gradient of <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{L}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{L}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{up}}=\mathcal{D}X_{L}^{\text{down}}\odot\text{silu}(Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}),\quad\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}=\mathcal{D}X_{L}^{\text{down}}\odot Y_{L}^{\text{up}}\odot\text{silu}^{\prime}(Y_{L}^{\text{gate}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext>silu</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>silu</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{up}}=\mathcal{D}X_{L}^{\text{down}}\odot\text{silu}(Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}),\quad\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}=\mathcal{D}X_{L}^{\text{down}}\odot Y_{L}^{\text{up}}\odot\text{silu}^{\prime}(Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">For the other layers, the corresponding gradient of activations should combine the back-propagated gradients and the historical gradients. Thus it holds that:</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E24X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{up}}\mathcal{D}Y_{l+1}^{\text{up}}+\mathcal{D}X_{l}^{\text{down}}\odot\text{silu}(Y_{l}^{\text{gate}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext>silu</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{up}}\mathcal{D}Y_{l+1}^{\text{up}}+\mathcal{D}X_{l}^{\text{down}}\odot\text{silu}(Y_{l}^{\text{gate}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E24Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{gate}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{gate}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{gate}}\mathcal{D}Y_{l+1}^{\text{gate}}+\mathcal{D}X_{l}^{\text{down}}\odot Y_{l}^{\text{up}}\odot\text{silu}^{\prime}(Y_{l}^{\text{gate}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>silu</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{gate}}\mathcal{D}Y_{l+1}^{\text{gate}}+\mathcal{D}X_{l}^{\text{down}}\odot Y_{l}^{\text{up}}\odot\text{silu}^{\prime}(Y_{l}^{\text{gate}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Then the gradient for parameter of up-projection and gate in the first layer can be computed by:</p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{O}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{2}^{\text{O}}\mathcal{D}Y_{2}^{\text{O}}+\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{up}}(W_{1}^{\text{up}})+\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{gate}}(W_{1}^{\text{gate}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{2}^{\text{O}}\mathcal{D}Y_{2}^{\text{O}}+\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{up}}(W_{1}^{\text{up}})+\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{gate}}(W_{1}^{\text{gate}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(Y_{1}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{up}},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{gate}}=(Y_{1}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{gate}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>up</mtext></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>gate</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>gate</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(Y_{1}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{up}},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{gate}}=(Y_{1}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{gate}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=2,3,\cdots,L-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=2,3,\cdots,L-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the gradient for parameter of up-projection and gate in the layer <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed by:</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{O}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{O}}\mathcal{D}Y_{l+1}^{\text{O}}+\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{up}}(A_{l}^{\text{up}}B_{l}^{\text{up}})+\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{gate}}(A_{l}^{\text{gate}}B_{l}^{\text{gate}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{O}}\mathcal{D}Y_{l+1}^{\text{O}}+\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{up}}(A_{l}^{\text{up}}B_{l}^{\text{up}})+\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{gate}}(A_{l}^{\text{gate}}B_{l}^{\text{gate}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E26Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(Y_{l}^{\text{O}}A_{l}^{\text{up}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{up}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{up}}=(Y_{l}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(Y_{l}^{\text{O}}A_{l}^{\text{up}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{up}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{up}}=(Y_{l}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E26Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{down}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{down}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(Y_{l}^{\text{O}}A_{l}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{down}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{down}}=(Y_{l}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{down}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(Y_{l}^{\text{O}}A_{l}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{down}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{down}}=(Y_{l}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{down}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p">The gradient for parameter of up-projection and gate in the last layer can be computed by:</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E27X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{O}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{up}}(A_{L}^{\text{up}}B_{L}^{\text{up}})+\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}(A_{L}^{\text{gate}}B_{L}^{\text{gate}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{up}}(A_{L}^{\text{up}}B_{L}^{\text{up}})+\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{gate}}(A_{L}^{\text{gate}}B_{L}^{\text{gate}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E27Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{L}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{L}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(Y_{L}^{\text{O}}A_{L}^{\text{up}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{up}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{L}^{\text{up}}=(Y_{L}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{L}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(Y_{L}^{\text{O}}A_{L}^{\text{up}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{up}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{L}^{\text{up}}=(Y_{L}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{L}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E27Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{L}^{\text{down}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{L}^{\text{down}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(Y_{L}^{\text{O}}A_{L}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{down}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{L}^{\text{down}}=(Y_{L}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{L}^{\text{down}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>O</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>down</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(Y_{L}^{\text{O}}A_{L}^{\text{down}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{L}^{\text{down}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{L}^{\text{down}}=(Y_{L}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{L}^{\text{down}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Then for the first layer, the gradients for parameter of output layer in attention can be computed by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{1}^{\text{h}}=\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{O}}(W_{1}^{\text{O}})^{\top},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{O}}=(\text{Att}_{1}^{\text{h}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{O}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mn>1</mn><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mn>1</mn><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{1}^{\text{h}}=\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{O}}(W_{1}^{\text{O}})^{\top},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{O}}=(\text{Att}_{1}^{\text{h}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{O}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">For the other layers, the gradients can be computed by:</p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{O}}(A_{l}^{\text{O}}B_{l}^{\text{O}})^{\top},\quad\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{O}}=(\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}A_{l}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{O}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{O}}=(\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{O}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>O</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{O}}(A_{l}^{\text{O}}B_{l}^{\text{O}})^{\top},\quad\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{O}}=(\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}A_{l}^{\text{O}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{O}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{O}}=(\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{O}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Next, the gradient for <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}=\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}(Y^{\text{V}}_{l})^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}=\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}(Y^{\text{V}}_{l})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Then for the last layer, the gradient for the activation <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\text{Q}}_{L},Y^{\text{K}}_{L},Y^{\text{V}}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\text{Q}}_{L},Y^{\text{K}}_{L},Y^{\text{V}}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained by:</p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{V}}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{V}}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\text{Att}_{L}^{\text{s}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{L}^{\text{h}},\quad\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{Q}}_{L}=\left[\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{L}^{\text{s}}\odot\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{h}}\text{softmax}^{\prime}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{L}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right)\right]Y^{\text{K}}_{L}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Att</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>s</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>Att</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>h</mtext></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>Q</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>Att</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>s</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>softmax</mtext><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mtext>Att</mtext><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>K</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\text{Att}_{L}^{\text{s}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{L}^{\text{h}},\quad\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{Q}}_{L}=\left[\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{L}^{\text{s}}\odot\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{h}}\text{softmax}^{\prime}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{L}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right)\right]Y^{\text{K}}_{L},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{K}}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{K}}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{L}^{\text{s}}\odot\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{h}}\text{softmax}^{\prime}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{L}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right)\right]^{\top}Y^{\text{Q}}_{L}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>L</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mtext>Att</mtext><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>L</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{L}^{\text{s}}\odot\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{h}}\text{softmax}^{\prime}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{L}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right)\right]^{\top}Y^{\text{Q}}_{L}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.3" class="ltx_p">And the gradients of the other layers can be obtained by:</p>
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E32X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{V}}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{V}}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{V}}\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{V}}_{l+1}+(\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{V}}\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{V}}_{l+1}+(\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{h}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E32Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{Q}}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{Q}}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{Q}}\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{Q}}_{l+1}+\left[\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}\odot\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{h}}\text{softmax}^{\prime}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{l}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right)\right]Y^{\text{K}}_{l}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mtext>Att</mtext><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{Q}}\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{Q}}_{l+1}+\left[\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}\odot\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{h}}\text{softmax}^{\prime}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{l}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right)\right]Y^{\text{K}}_{l},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E32Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{K}}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{K}}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{K}}\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{K}}_{l+1}+\left[\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}\odot\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{h}}\text{softmax}^{\prime}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{l}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right)\right]^{\top}Y^{\text{Q}}_{l}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext>Att</mtext><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mtext>Att</mtext><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msubsup><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{l+1}^{\text{K}}\mathcal{D}Y^{\text{K}}_{l+1}+\left[\mathcal{D}\text{Att}_{l}^{\text{s}}\odot\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{h}}\text{softmax}^{\prime}\left(\dfrac{\widetilde{\text{Att}}_{l}^{\text{s}}}{\sqrt{h}}\right)\right]^{\top}Y^{\text{Q}}_{l}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the gradients of the weights for query, key, and value in the first layer can be obtained as:</p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E33X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{Q}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{Q}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(X_{1})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{Q}},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{K}}=(X_{1})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{K}},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{V}}=(X_{1})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{V}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(X_{1})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{Q}},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{K}}=(X_{1})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{K}},\quad\mathcal{D}W_{1}^{\text{V}}=(X_{1})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{V}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E33Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}X_{1}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}X_{1}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{Q}}(W_{1}^{\text{Q}})^{\top}+\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{K}}(W_{1}^{\text{K}})^{\top}+\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{V}}(W_{1}^{\text{V}})^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{Q}}(W_{1}^{\text{Q}})^{\top}+\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{K}}(W_{1}^{\text{K}})^{\top}+\mathcal{D}Y_{1}^{\text{V}}(W_{1}^{\text{V}})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p">the gradients of the weights for query, key, and value in the other layers can be obtained as:</p>
<table id="A1.E34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E34X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{Q}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{Q}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{Q}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{Q}},\quad\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{K}}=(X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{K}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{K}},\quad\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{V}}=(X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{V}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{V}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{Q}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{Q}},\quad\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{K}}=(X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{K}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{K}},\quad\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{V}}=(X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{V}})^{\top}\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{V}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E34Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{Q}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{Q}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(X_{l})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{Q}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{K}}=(X_{l})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{K}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{V}}=(X_{l})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{V}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(X_{l})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{Q}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{K}}=(X_{l})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{K}},\quad\mathcal{D}A_{l}^{\text{V}}=(X_{l})^{\top}\mathcal{D}B_{l}^{\text{V}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E34Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}X_{l}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}X_{l}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{Q}}(A_{l}^{\text{Q}}B_{l}^{\text{Q}})^{\top}+\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{K}}(A_{l}^{\text{K}}B_{l}^{\text{K}})^{\top}+\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{V}}(A_{l}^{\text{V}}B_{l}^{\text{V}})^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{Q}}(A_{l}^{\text{Q}}B_{l}^{\text{Q}})^{\top}+\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{K}}(A_{l}^{\text{K}}B_{l}^{\text{K}})^{\top}+\mathcal{D}Y_{l}^{\text{V}}(A_{l}^{\text{V}}B_{l}^{\text{V}})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Computation analysis without re-computation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we present the computation analysis of <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net </span>with re-computation in detail. The brief analysis is shown in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Complexity analysis without re-computation ‣ 4 Complexity analysis ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. To begin with, we should remind that the matrices production with size <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times r</annotation></semantics></math> need <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2mnr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2mnr</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the first layer, the computation of forward propagation is totally the same as full-rank training. Thus the computation FLOPs can be computed by:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention Q, K, V: Three matrices productions with size <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6sh^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6sh^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention SDP: One matrices production with size <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times s</annotation></semantics></math> and one matrices production with size <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4s^{2}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4s^{2}h</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention O: One matrices production with size <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2sh^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sh^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FFN gate and up: Two matrices productions with size <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times h_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times h_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4shh_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4shh_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FFN down: One matrices production with size <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\text{ff}}\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\text{ff}}\times h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2shh_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2shh_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the computation complexity of the first layer is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8sh^{2}+4s^{2}h+6shh_{\text{ff}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8sh^{2}+4s^{2}h+6shh_{\text{ff}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the other layers, we can omit the cross-layer residual operations as its complexity is a lower-order term. Thus, the computation complexity of different components are as follow:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention Q, K, V: Three matrices productions with size <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times r</annotation></semantics></math>, and three matrices productions with size <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12shr</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention SDP: The same as that of the first layer, <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4s^{2}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4s^{2}h</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention O: One matrices production with size <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times r</annotation></semantics></math>, and one matrices production with size <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4shr</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FFN gate and up: Two matrices productions with size <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times r</annotation></semantics></math>, and two matrices productions with size <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times h_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times h_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FFN down: One matrices production with size <math id="A1.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times r</annotation></semantics></math>, and one matrices production with size <math id="A1.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times h_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times h_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I2.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs in total.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the computation complexity of the other layers is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16shr+4s^{2}h+6sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16shr+4s^{2}h+6sr(h+h_{\text{ff}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the total computation complexity in the forward-propagation is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{8sh^{2}+4s^{2}h+6shh_{\text{ff}}}_{\mathrm{FLOPs\ in\ the\ first\ layer}}+(L-1)(\underbrace{16shr+4s^{2}h+6sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})}_{\mathrm{FLOPs\ in\ the\ other\ layers}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>FLOPs</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>in</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>the</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>first</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>layer</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>FLOPs</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>in</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>the</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>other</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>layers</mi></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{8sh^{2}+4s^{2}h+6shh_{\text{ff}}}_{\mathrm{FLOPs\ in\ the\ first\ layer}}+(L-1)(\underbrace{16shr+4s^{2}h+6sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})}_{\mathrm{FLOPs\ in\ the\ other\ layers}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backward-propagation. </span>For backward-propagation. It can be obtained that the toatl computation FLOPs is twice of that in forward-propagation if we omit the lower-order terms. Thus, the total computation complexity in the forward-propagation is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{16sh^{2}+8s^{2}h+12shh_{\text{ff}}}_{\mathrm{FLOPs\ in\ the\ first\ layer}}+(L-1)(\underbrace{32shr+8s^{2}h+12sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})}_{\mathrm{FLOPs\ in\ the\ other\ layers}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>FLOPs</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>in</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>the</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>first</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>layer</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>FLOPs</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>in</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>the</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>other</mi><mo lspace="0.400em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>layers</mi></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{16sh^{2}+8s^{2}h+12shh_{\text{ff}}}_{\mathrm{FLOPs\ in\ the\ first\ layer}}+(L-1)(\underbrace{32shr+8s^{2}h+12sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})}_{\mathrm{FLOPs\ in\ the\ other\ layers}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we can obtain that the total computation of <span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net </span>for one gradient step is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 24sh^{2}+12s^{2}h+18shh_{\text{ff}}+(L-1)(48shr+12s^{2}h+18sr(h+h_{\text{ff}}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>48</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 24sh^{2}+12s^{2}h+18shh_{\text{ff}}+(L-1)(48shr+12s^{2}h+18sr(h+h_{\text{ff}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Computation and memory analysis with re-computation</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Activation memory and re-computation analysis of <span id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net</span></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present the computation and memory analysis of <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net </span>with re-computation strategy which has been shown in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 CR-Net with activation-efficient re-compuation ‣ 3 CR-Net: Cross-layer residual network for LLM pre-training ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.1 </span>Memory analysis</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first present the analysis of memory overheads of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net </span>with re-computation. In fact, the following variables need to be stored:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Inputs for each layer: <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Lsh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Lsh</annotation></semantics></math> parameters in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Low-rank outputs <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}^{\text{P}}A_{l}^{\text{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}^{\text{P}}A_{l}^{\text{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all linear layers except the first transformer layer: <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7(L-1)sr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7(L-1)sr</annotation></semantics></math> parameters in total.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Linear outputs <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}^{\text{P}}A_{l}^{\text{P}}B_{l}^{\text{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}^{\text{P}}A_{l}^{\text{P}}B_{l}^{\text{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5|\mathcal{A}|sh+2|\mathcal{A}|sh_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5|\mathcal{A}|sh+2|\mathcal{A}|sh_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> parameters in total.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the total memory overhead of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net </span>with re-computation is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(L+5|\mathcal{A}|)sh+2|\mathcal{A}|sh_{\text{ff}}+7(L-1)sr." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(L+5|\mathcal{A}|)sh+2|\mathcal{A}|sh_{\text{ff}}+7(L-1)sr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.2 </span>Computation analysis</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then we present the analysis of re-computation overheads of <span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net</span>, which can be computed by:</p>
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention Q, K, V: If <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, no FLOPs need as all the activation with is necessary for the backward-propagation has been stored. If <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l+1\not\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l+1\not\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, the linear combination between low-rank output and the matrix <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}^{\text{Q}},B_{l}^{\text{K}},B_{l}^{\text{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}^{\text{Q}},B_{l}^{\text{K}},B_{l}^{\text{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the stored matrices <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{Q}},X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{K}},X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>K</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>V</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{Q}},X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{K}},X_{l}A_{l}^{\text{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. The shape of the multiplied matrices are <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times h</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Thus the total FLOPs is <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6(L-|\mathcal{A}|)shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6(L-|\mathcal{A}|)shr</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention SDP: All the layers should take one matrices production with size <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times s</annotation></semantics></math> and one matrices production with size <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times h</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the total FLOPs is <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4Ls^{2}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4Ls^{2}h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention O: It is the same as the discussion for attention Q, K, V. Thus the total FLOPs is <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(L-|\mathcal{A}|)shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(L-|\mathcal{A}|)shr</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FFN gate and up: It is the same as the discussion for attention Q, K, V. Note that the size of the multiplied matrices are <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rtimesh_{ff}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rtimesh_{ff}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, thus the total FLOPs is <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4(L-|\mathcal{A}|)sh_{\text{ff}}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4(L-|\mathcal{A}|)sh_{\text{ff}}r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FFN down: It is the same as the discussion for attention Q, K, V. Note that the size of the multiplied matrices are <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rtimesh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rtimesh</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, thus the total FLOPs is <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(L-|\mathcal{A}|)shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(L-|\mathcal{A}|)shr</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the total re-computation complexity is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 10(L-|\mathcal{A}|)shr+4(L-|\mathcal{A}|)sh_{\text{ff}}r+4Ls^{2}h." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 10(L-|\mathcal{A}|)shr+4(L-|\mathcal{A}|)sh_{\text{ff}}r+4Ls^{2}h.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Re-computation complexity of CoLA-M</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Complexity analysis with re-computation ‣ 4 Complexity analysis ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents the recomputation complexity of activation-effective approaches, including CoLA-M. In fact, the re-computation complexity of CoLA-M can be obtained by the similar analysis process of <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net</span> in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1.SSS2" title="B.1.2 Computation analysis ‣ B.1 Activation memory and re-computation analysis of CR-Net ‣ Appendix B Computation and memory analysis with re-computation ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1.2</span></a>. The total re-computation complexity for one gradient step of CoLA-M is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 10Lshr+4Lsh_{\text{ff}}r+4Ls^{2}h." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 10Lshr+4Lsh_{\text{ff}}r+4Ls^{2}h.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When taking the intermediate dimension <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\text{ff}}=8h/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\text{ff}}=8h/3</annotation></semantics></math>, the total re-computation complexity for one gradient step of CoLA-M is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 20.67Lshr+4Ls^{2}h." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>20.67</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 20.67Lshr+4Ls^{2}h.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>, the re-computation FLOPs of CoLA-M is obtained as the re-computation only takes half of total flops of linear layers with the assumption. However, for gate and up-projection layer, the production of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}^{\text{gate}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}^{\text{gate}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}^{\text{gate}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}^{\text{gate}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math>) takes <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2shr</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs while production of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}^{\text{gate}}A_{l}^{\text{gate}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}^{\text{gate}}A_{l}^{\text{gate}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}^{\text{up}}A_{l}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}^{\text{up}}A_{l}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}^{\text{gate}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h_{\text{ff}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}^{\text{gate}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h_{\text{ff}}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}^{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}^{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math>) takes <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2sh_{\text{ff}}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sh_{\text{ff}}r</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs. For down-projection layer, the production of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times h_{\text{ff}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times h_{\text{ff}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h_{\text{ff}}\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{h_{\text{ff}}\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2sh_{\text{ff}}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2sh_{\text{ff}}r</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs while production of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}^{\text{down}}A_{l}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}^{\text{down}}A_{l}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}^{\text{down}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2shr</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs. Thus, the computational FLOPs of the FFN are not given by <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3sh_{\text{ff}}r+3shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3sh_{\text{ff}}r+3shr</annotation></semantics></math>—half of the total FLOPs—but rather by <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4sh_{\text{ff}}r+2shr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4sh_{\text{ff}}r+2shr</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Theoretical insight: Residual Subtraction Improves Low-Rank Approximation</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present a theoretical insight to explain the phenomenon we observed in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Observation: previous-Layer and low-Rank term present a better activation approximation ‣ 3 CR-Net: Cross-layer residual network for LLM pre-training ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. To begin with, we present an assumption of the cosine similarity of the activations for adjacent layers.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Cosine similarity of adjacent activations)<span id="Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=2,3,\cdots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=2,3,\cdots,L</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as the activation of the linear of position <span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">P</span> for the <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer. There exists a constant <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\langle Y_{l}^{\text{P}},Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\rangle_{F}}{\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\|_{F}\cdot\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\|_{F}}\geq 1-\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\langle Y_{l}^{\text{P}},Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\rangle_{F}}{\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\|_{F}\cdot\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\|_{F}}\geq 1-\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the inner production of matrices induced by Frobenius norm.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Cosine similarity of adjacent activations). ‣ Appendix C Theoretical insight: Residual Subtraction Improves Low-Rank Approximation ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> illustrates that the activation of Transformer-based models have a high cosine similarity. Such a characteristic have been observed in different kinds of models and different positions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, we present the definition of the stable rank.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stable rank)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the stable rank of <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> (represented as <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(A)</annotation></semantics></math>) is denoted as the ratio between the square of Frobenius norm of <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and the square of <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm of <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(A)=\dfrac{||A||_{F}^{2}}{||A||_{2}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(A)=\dfrac{||A||_{F}^{2}}{||A||_{2}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The stable rank can be also defined as the ratio between the quadratic sum of singular values and the square of the maximum singular value.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then we can obtain the theorem that the approximation in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 Observation: previous-Layer and low-Rank term present a better activation approximation ‣ 3 CR-Net: Cross-layer residual network for LLM pre-training ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) is a better estimator than low-rank approximation, especially with a small rank <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Cosine similarity of adjacent activations). ‣ Appendix C Theoretical insight: Residual Subtraction Improves Low-Rank Approximation ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds. Then there exists <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that the approximation <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 Observation: previous-Layer and low-Rank term present a better activation approximation ‣ 3 CR-Net: Cross-layer residual network for LLM pre-training ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) has a lower error than the direct low-rank approximation <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">LR</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> by a properly-selected <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, it holds that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\leq\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})\right\|_{F}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">LR</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\leq\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})\right\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we denote <math id="Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> as the <math id="Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th singular value of a matrix, which is listed in descending order. Then, the term <math id="Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}=\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}-\beta Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}=\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-2\beta\left\langle Y_{l}^{\text{P}},Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\rangle+\beta^{2}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}=\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}-\beta Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}=\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-2\beta\left\langle Y_{l}^{\text{P}},Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\rangle+\beta^{2}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}=2\beta\left\langle Y_{l}^{\text{P}},Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\rangle-\beta^{2}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}=2\beta\left\langle Y_{l}^{\text{P}},Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\rangle-\beta^{2}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Weyl’s inequality, the <math id="Thmtheorem1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th singular value of <math id="Thmtheorem1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{l}^{\text{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{l}^{\text{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})-\sigma_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}})|\leq\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}-\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\leq\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})-\sigma_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}})|\leq\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}-\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\leq\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, it holds that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E45X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})-\sigma^{2}_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})-\sigma^{2}_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})-\sigma_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}))(\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})+\sigma_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})-\sigma_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}))(\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})+\sigma_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E45Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}(\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})+\sigma_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}(\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})+\sigma_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E45Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left(2\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})+\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left(2\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})+\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking summation over <math id="Thmtheorem1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\cdots,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\cdots,r</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq r\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq r\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E46X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{r}\left(\sigma^{2}_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})-\sigma^{2}_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}})\right)^{2}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{r}\left(\sigma^{2}_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})-\sigma^{2}_{i}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}})\right)^{2}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left(2\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})+\beta r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left(2\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})+\beta r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E46Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left(2\sqrt{r}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}^{2}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})\right)^{1/2}+\beta r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left(2\sqrt{r}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}^{2}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})\right)^{1/2}+\beta r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E46Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left(2\sqrt{r}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}+\beta r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left(2\sqrt{r}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}+\beta r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality is due to Cauchy-Schwarz inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we consider the approximation error for <math id="Thmtheorem1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>LR</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can obtain that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E47X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>LR</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E47Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\left\|\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}^{2}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}})\right)-\left(\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}^{2}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\left\|\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}^{2}(\Delta_{\beta}Y_{l}^{\text{P}})\right)-\left(\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}^{2}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E47Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-2\beta\left\langle Y_{l}^{\text{P}},Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\rangle+\beta^{2}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+2\beta\sqrt{r}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}+\beta^{2}r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\beta\left\langle Y_{l}^{\text{P}},Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\rangle+\beta^{2}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+2\beta\sqrt{r}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}+\beta^{2}r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E47Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-2\beta(1-\varepsilon)\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}+\beta^{2}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+2\beta\sqrt{r}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}+\beta^{2}r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\beta(1-\varepsilon)\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}+\beta^{2}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+2\beta\sqrt{r}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}+\beta^{2}r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E47Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta^{2}\left(\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)-2\beta\left((1-\varepsilon)\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}-\sqrt{r}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta^{2}\left(\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)-2\beta\left((1-\varepsilon)\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}-\sqrt{r}\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E47Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47Xe.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta^{2}\left(\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)-2\beta\left((1-\varepsilon)\sqrt{\varphi(Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}})}-\sqrt{r}\right)\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta^{2}\left(\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)-2\beta\left((1-\varepsilon)\sqrt{\varphi(Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}})}-\sqrt{r}\right)\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality is due to Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Cosine similarity of adjacent activations). ‣ Appendix C Theoretical insight: Residual Subtraction Improves Low-Rank Approximation ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="Thmtheorem1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}=(1-\varepsilon)^{2}\varphi(Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}=(1-\varepsilon)^{2}\varphi(Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Thmtheorem1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\leq\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>LR</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\leq\left\|{Y}_{l}^{\text{P}}-\text{LR}_{r}({Y}_{l}^{\text{P}})\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> holds if</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta=\dfrac{\left((1-\varepsilon)\sqrt{\varphi(Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}})}-\sqrt{r}\right)\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}}{\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta=\dfrac{\left((1-\varepsilon)\sqrt{\varphi(Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}})}-\sqrt{r}\right)\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}\left\|Y_{l}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}}{\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{F}^{2}+r\left\|Y_{l-1}^{\text{P}}\right\|_{2}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we finish the proof of this theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental details and additional experiments</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Experimental details for the observation of cross-layer low-rank structure</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To empirically validate the cross-layer low-rank structure in different models and training periods., we conducted comparative experiments by fine-tuning the pre-trained LLaMA-3 8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> and GPT-2-small <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> models. And we also pre-training a LLaMA-3 8B model as well as a model built from Qwen-3-MoE model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>. The hyperparameter configurations for Qwen-3-based model is as Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ D.1 Experimental details for the observation of cross-layer low-rank structure ‣ Appendix D Experimental details and additional experiments ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. We use the TinyShakespeare dataset for both pre-training and fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We subsequently quantified the activation approximation errors through two distinct methodologies: (a) direct low-rank estimation <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{LR}_{r}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>LR</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>l</mi><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{LR}_{r}(Y_{l}^{\text{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> and (b) matrix recovery via Equation (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 Observation: previous-Layer and low-Rank term present a better activation approximation ‣ 3 CR-Net: Cross-layer residual network for LLM pre-training ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). The rank parameter <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.25h,0.5h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.25h,0.5h</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. And for <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta_{0}}^{\text{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mtext>P</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Y}_{l,\beta_{0}}^{\text{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> definited in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 Observation: previous-Layer and low-Rank term present a better activation approximation ‣ 3 CR-Net: Cross-layer residual network for LLM pre-training ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), the scaling factor <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned from <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,0.2,0.4,0.6,0.8,1,2,3,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,0.2,0.4,0.6,0.8,1,2,3,5\}</annotation></semantics></math>. And the other hyperparameters can be referred from Table <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ D.1 Experimental details for the observation of cross-layer low-rank structure ‣ Appendix D Experimental details and additional experiments ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Hyperparameter configurations for Qwen-3-based model with MoE architecture.</figcaption>
