</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.6 </span>Pre-training with longer sequence and more training tokens</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To align with the basic experimental setup of existing efficient frameworks for LLMs pre-training like LoRA and GaLore, we follow the setup in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite> and use a short sequence length, to validate the pre-training performance in long training tokens as well as more training tokens. We pre-trained LLaMA-2 models using the C4-en dataset with maximum sequence length set to 2048. The total training tokens are more than <math id="A4.SS2.SSS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="22\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22\times</annotation></semantics></math> the parameter size to follow the Chinchilla scaling law <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>. As shown in Table <a href="#A4.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ D.2.5 Experimental setting and additional results for the ablations ‣ D.2 Experimental details for C4 pre-training tasks ‣ Appendix D Experimental details and additional experiments ‣ CR-Net: Scaling Parameter-Efficient Training with Cross-Layer Low-Rank Structure" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, <span id="A4.SS2.SSS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CR-Net </span>outperforms GaLore in this scenario.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T13" class="ltx_table">
